  "goodToKnow": "Bisweilen means at times or now and then: Bisweilen regnet es tagelang. It's literary and slightly old-fashioned, found in novels, essays and quality newspapers; in everyday speech, Germans say manchmal, ab und zu or hin und wieder. Other elegant alternatives: zuweilen, mitunter, gelegentlich. It's built from bis and Weile (a while), like derweil and Langeweile."
